# Full Migration Plan: [supervisor](file:///home/sudais/projects/FYPILOT-BACKEND/app/repositories/group_repository.py#378-396) → `faculty`

## Goal
Rename the [supervisor](file:///home/sudais/projects/FYPILOT-BACKEND/app/repositories/group_repository.py#378-396) role to `faculty`. Faculty is the umbrella identity — the `is_supervisor` and `is_jury` boolean flags on the faculty profile determine what a faculty member can do:
- **`is_supervisor=True`** → Can supervise groups, appear in student explore, accept supervision requests
- **`is_jury=True`** → Can serve as jury in evaluations  
- **Both `True`** → Default on registration (can do both)
- **Neither `True`** → Faculty is effectively inactive

All three (faculty, supervisor, jury) share the **same profile table** and basic functions (profile, announcements, etc). The flags only gate *specific* features.

---

## Key Clarifications from User

> [!NOTE]
> - **Keep `all_supervisors`** in `target_role_enum` alongside new `all_faculty`
> - **Bulk registration** = "Faculty Registration" (not supervisor). Both `is_supervisor` and `is_jury` flags default to `True`
> - **Admin list** shows all faculty with their flags (supervisor, jury, or both)
> - **`groups.supervisor_id`** stays as-is (it means "the faculty member supervising this group")
> - **URL prefixes** will change from `/supervisors` to `/faculty`

---

## Phase 1: Database Migration (Alembic)

```sql
-- 1A. Rename user role enum value
ALTER TYPE user_role_enum RENAME VALUE 'supervisor' TO 'faculty';

-- 1B. Rename tables
ALTER TABLE supervisors RENAME TO faculty;
ALTER TABLE supervisor_domains RENAME TO faculty_domains;
ALTER TABLE supervisor_industries RENAME TO faculty_industries;

-- 1C. Announcement enum: ADD new value, keep old one
ALTER TYPE announcement_role_enum RENAME VALUE 'supervisor' TO 'faculty';
-- target_role_enum: keep 'all_supervisors', add 'all_faculty'
ALTER TYPE target_role_enum ADD VALUE 'all_faculty';

-- 1D. Bulk import enum
-- The bulk_import target_role_enum 'supervisor' → 'faculty'
ALTER TYPE target_role_enum RENAME VALUE 'supervisor' TO 'faculty';
```

> [!WARNING]
> `groups.supervisor_id`, `groups.cosupervisor_ids` — FK columns **stay as-is**. They reference `faculty.user_id` now (table renamed) but their column names remain semantically correct.

